From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] Ocarina parser lifetime and macro atomicity: the split decision is made on the words the
 parser runs, a failed front macro reports the writes it sent, an undefined render condition skips its draws, device
 addresses past the device space read as unmapped

Found from crash-20261108-203326 (Ocarina, 109 s, SIGSEGV in GPUBack, ReadBlockImpl):

1. DmaPusher::SplitContinuesHere read guest memory (ReadBlockUnsafe) to decide whether an entry
   continues the method the entry before left open, while Step parses the submit copy, a flushed
   read or the list copy. The game refills its command ring; the decision and the parse could see
   different words, and a fresh header was taken as the data of an open method (the log shows a
   macro called with the single parameter a0040e02, a header). DecideSplitOnWords decides on the
   span ProcessCommands will run (EDEN_NX2_SPLIT_PARSE_CHECK, unchanged otherwise).
2. EDEN_NX2_DESYNC_FIX (0408/0411) stays off with EDEN_NX2_SPLIT_PARSE_CHECK set; it now runs with
   it (it stays off with JUNK_GUARD / PARK_SPLIT_METHODS, whose parses its walk does not model).
3. Maxwell3D::FrontRunMacro's failure line says how many register writes the failed call already sent.
   (Holding the writes back until the call succeeds was tried and removed: FrontWrite has side effects the
   macro reads back - const_buffer.offset, load_mme pointers - and a macro looping on them hung at boot.)
4. A render-condition mode no hardware defines skips its draws for Ocarina (EDEN_NX2_BAD_COND_SKIP
   =0/1) instead of drawing with the rest of the garbage state. Other titles are unchanged.
5. DeviceMemoryManager::GetPointer / WalkBlock / ReadBlock check the device address space; a GPU page
   table entry past it (stale or corrupt) read tracked_entries out of bounds and returned a wild
   pointer. MemoryManager::ReadBlockImpl logs the first 16 such reads with the GPU address. This
   contains the fault; it does not explain how the entry came to be wrong (see the crash report).
